# Every environment variable the gate battery is allowed to see, one KEY=VALUE
# per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until 2026-08-17 the local runner inherited the whole
# invoking shell, so the verdict of the required `local-gates` status was a
# function of (commit, operator) rather than of the commit alone, and nothing
# declared or recorded the operator half. Concretely: BROTHERSBE_VAULT is set in
# a personal Claude Code settings file on the maintainer's machine, and the
# twelve vault-fed checks in tools/sbe_score.py therefore ran with real data
# locally and returned NO-DATA on GitHub Actions, whose workflow never set it.
# The same commit scored 10 PASS / 2 FAIL / 3 NO-DATA locally and 3 PASS /
# 0 FAIL / 12 NO-DATA in CI. The gate was red on this machine and green in the
# cloud, and neither reviewer nor receipt could see why.
#
# What a CI container actually gave was not Linux and not the cloud: it was an
# environment built from a reviewed file instead of inherited from a person.
# This file is that reviewed file. Default deny, declared allow. Anything not
# named here is stripped before any gate command runs, and the count of what was
# stripped is printed and written into the receipt.
#
# THE INHERITED MINIMUM is not listed here because it is not repository policy:
# PATH, HOME, TMPDIR and the locale identify the machine, and the runner passes
# them through and records them. Everything else starts empty.
#
# TO ADD A VARIABLE: name it here with the value the battery should see, and say
# in a comment why the battery needs it. A variable that changes what a check
# MEASURES belongs in this file or nowhere; setting it in a shell profile puts
# the verdict back under the operator's feet, which is the defect this closes.

# Declared by the gates job of .github/workflows/brothersbe-gates.yml. Empty
# means "search the whole checkout for dossiers" rather than "no dossier root",
# and the empty value is deliberate: see that workflow's own comment.
SBE_DOSSIER_ROOT=

# DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and this absence is the point rather than an omission:
#
#   BROTHERSBE_VAULT       twelve checks in tools/sbe_score.py read an external
#                          Obsidian vault through it. Those checks measure the
#                          OPERATOR (cache warm-read ratios over recent sessions,
#                          how promptly corrections were processed, whether a
#                          session log exists per active day). They are real
#                          signal and they are not facts about this repository,
#                          so they cannot decide whether this commit may merge.
#                          `cache-economy` in particular reads finished session
#                          records that no commit can alter, so wiring it to a
#                          commit gate makes the gate un-winnable by code.
#                          Absent here, those checks report NO-DATA, which is
#                          exactly what they reported under Actions, and NO-DATA
#                          never blocks and is never read as a pass.
#                          To see them, run the operator report, which is one
#                          documented command in docs/LOCAL-VERIFICATION.md.
#
#   BROTHERSBE_REGISTRIES  same reasoning: fence-hygiene and budget-vs-tier read
#                          registries outside this repository.
#
#   SBE_CITATION_ROOT      unset, so citation-inventory uses its own default,
#                          which is the tree under test. Pointing it elsewhere
#                          would score a different codebase and report the
#                          verdict against this commit.
#
#   PYTHONPATH             an inherited PYTHONPATH can shadow a module under
#                          test with one from another checkout, which turns a
#                          green battery into a statement about the wrong code.

# Byte-compilation off. A stale .pyc has served deleted code to this estate
# before: a same-length edit reverted inside one second is invisible to the
# (mtime, size) check the interpreter uses, so it kept running code no longer on
# disk. A verification run must read the tree, not a cache of an earlier one.
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1

# SHELL, declared 2026-08-19 with a fixed value rather than inherited. `sbe
# doctor` REPORTS the environment, so its platform line reads "$SHELL" and
# prints "shell unknown; $SHELL is unset" when the variable is absent. With
# SHELL undeclared, that line was a function of (commit, operator): a book
# block regenerated at a developer's prompt matched there and differed inside
# this sandbox, which is exactly the non-determinism this file exists to
# remove. Declaring it fixes the value for every run instead of importing the
# operator's login shell, so the battery stays a function of the commit alone.
SHELL=/bin/bash
